// @run
// A DECLARATIONS-ONLY module, NAMED ON THE COMMAND LINE. It prints nothing, and that is the
// whole assertion: `passCheckTopLevel` refused a program with no functions and no start
// statements, so `export type Point = { x: i32, y: i32 }` was `vl check` rc 0 and
// `emitProgram: expected at least one top-level function or statement` (D1080).
//
// THE ENTRY POSITION WAS THE ONLY INGREDIENT. This very file is IMPORTED and used by
// ../declarations-only-import/entry.vl, which compiles and runs today and always did — so
// the compiler already agreed a types-only module is a legal module; it just could not be
// the one you name. A `loud emit reject` on a check-clean program is a clause-2 violation by
// construction.
//
// An empty wasm module is valid wasm, and every section the emitter writes is already gated
// on having something to write, so the pass now enforces nothing and its sibling root-level
// floor (`expected at least one top-level statement`, the ZERO-BYTE and comment-only case)
// went with it — two sentences for one refusal, of which only that one has no declaration to
// look at. Measured: the artifact for this file is `(module)` at 25 bytes and `wasm-opt -O3`
// validates it.
export type Point = { x: i32, y: i32 }
export type Id = i32
